592186512886 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)-4{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{6}{s}-\\frac{2}{s-4},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=\\frac{3}{s}+\\frac{1}{s-4}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,+\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,{e}^{4t}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186512886 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4d0a8858-fa20-5f8a-859e-5ff864dcdd44" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186512886 #edb/ref 1074 "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{6}{s}-\\frac{2}{s-4}\\} \\\\  & =6{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\}-2{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-4}\\} \\\\  & =6\\cdot 1-2{e}^{4\\cdot t} \\\\  & =6-2{e}^{4t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{3}{s}+\\frac{1}{s-4}\\} \\\\  & =3{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\}+{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-4}\\} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 1+{e}^{4\\cdot t} \\\\  & =3+{e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6-2{e}^{4t} \\\\ 3+{e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186512949 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186512784 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186512949 #edb/ref 1069 "q-331948" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186512949 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186512949 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)-2{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{2(2s-9)}{(s-1)(s-4)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=$ {{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186512949 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e1726d67-859b-50b6-a736-a3033ae62d0e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186512949 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{2{x}_{1}(t)-2{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-2L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+3L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-4=2{X}_{1}(s)-2{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-3=-{X}_{1}(s)+3{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$\n\nRewriting the system in standard form, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}(s-2){X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s)=4 \\\\ {X}_{1}(s)+(s-3){X}_{2}(s)=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the second equation, we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=3-(s-3){X}_{2}(s).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(s-2)[3-(s-3){X}_{2}(s)]+2{X}_{2}(s) & =4 \\\\ 3(s-2)-[(s-2)(s-3)-2]{X}_{2}(s) & =4 \\\\ -({s}^{2}-5s+4){X}_{2}(s) & =4-3(s-2) \\\\ -(s-1)(s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =-3s+10 \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{3s-10}{(s-1)(s-4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${X}_{1}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{X}_{1}(s) & =3-(s-3){X}_{2}(s) \\\\  & =3-(s-3)\\cdot \\frac{3s-10}{(s-1)(s-4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(s-1)(s-4)-(s-3)(3s-10)}{(s-1)(s-4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4s-18}{(s-1)(s-4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(2s-9)}{(s-1)(s-4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{2(2s-9)}{(s-1)(s-4)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{3s-10}{(s-1)(s-4)}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186512957 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186512729 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186512957 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186512756 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186512957 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186512771 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186512957 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186512834 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186512957 #edb/ref 1069 "q-332299" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186512957 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186512957 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{3}{s-1},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s-1}-\\frac{2}{s-4}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,{e}^{t}+\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,{e}^{4t}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186512957 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fafb126e-2901-5759-82dc-9622ce8bea50" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186512957 #edb/ref 1074 "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{3}{s-1}\\} \\\\  & =3\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}\\} \\\\  & =3{e}^{1\\cdot t} \\\\  & =3{e}^{t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}-\\frac{2}{s-4}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}\\}-2\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-4}\\} \\\\  & ={e}^{1\\cdot t}-2{e}^{4\\cdot t} \\\\  & ={e}^{t}-2{e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{t} \\\\ {e}^{t}-2{e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186512967 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186513017 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186512967 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "26340763-1380-5c53-9b3f-a306a2619910" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186512967 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186512886 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186512995 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186513011 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186512995 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "65a90e25-be65-5cd0-8609-0b9b0c234c64" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186512995 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186512949 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186513011 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186512967 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186513011 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a6a0b32e-eb09-5421-a596-3e6fd4b1cd5c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186513011 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186512957 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186513017 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ce979f69-9765-5453-b829-f640b5b3f02e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186513017 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186305035 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186513020 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186512995 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186513020 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d6c97440-18e1-5786-af73-8f601577d3eb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186513020 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186304963 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
